# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Review verdicts are per-reviewer working state, not a shared artifact.
# A published audit result is committed deliberately, not by accident.
evals/review/verdicts.jsonl

# Tooling caches
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Environment-specific secrets. Follows the convention used by the
# keleusma repository. The directory exists locally and is never tracked.
secret/

# Transient scratch files. The directory itself is tracked through its
# placeholder so that the path exists in a fresh clone.
tmp/*
!tmp/.gitkeep

# NOTE ON corpus/ AND sources/
#
# AMENDED 2026-09-24. corpus/ now holds DERIVED output and is ignored
# for the same reason a build directory is. The books under
# curriculum/books/ are the authored artifact, and a stream under
# corpus/ is rebuilt from them by tools/build_corpus.py under a chosen
# ordering. Tracking it would add bytes without adding auditability.
#
# The original 2026-09-23 direction was that generated corpus data be
# tracked, and it was taken when corpus/ was going to hold the authored
# records. It no longer does. The benefit that direction bought is
# unchanged and is now bought by the books instead.
#
# sources/ is NOT ignored. Terminal-stage literature is acquired rather
# than derived and cannot be rebuilt.
#
# Two consequences are recorded here so that they are not rediscovered
# later by surprise.
#
# 1. Size. The host volume had 57 GiB free of 926 GiB at project
#    creation. A corpus at pretraining scale will exceed that. Git
#    Large File Storage is installed on this machine but has NOT been
#    configured for this repository. This amendment removes most of
#    that exposure, since the derived stream is the large artifact.
#
# 2. Provenance. Every record is still reviewable and attributable
#    through history, through the book that holds it.

corpus/*
!corpus/.gitkeep
!corpus/README.md
